      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the body say what goes wrong without the patch? As far as I can see there are two cases.\n\nThe type1 backend, which GKI builds in because `VFIO_CONTAINER` selects `VFIO_IOMMU_TYPE1` on arm64, pins `current-\u003emm` in `vfio_pin_pages_remote()` and maps a whole kernel page for each pinned page in `vfio_iommu_map()`, but the 4KB pages of a 16KB range can map slices of different kernel pages. And `vfio_platform_mmap_mmio()` maps MMIO past the end of a region when `vm_slice_off !\u003d 0`.\n\nThat would also explain why the container ioctl and device `mmap()` are checked: they cover fds that a native process passes on. \"Keep P3S page-size selection and native VFIO MMIO geometry unchanged\" only says what doesn\u0027t change.\n\nAlso, could the subject say \"4KB processes\" rather than \"PPPS host APIs\"? PPPS is the old abbreviation for P3S, and \"4KB processes\" would match aosp/4368079.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4988ff901d7c9635d69338a4c41cf65473605672",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a73c649a_b75cd277",
        "filename": "drivers/vfio/container.c",
