      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T06:57:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could these checks use `p3s_4k_unsupported()` (aosp/4366134) instead of `mm_is_p3s_4k()`? It logs the refusal with the function name, so refusals hit in production can be identified, and aosp/4368076 and aosp/4368079 use it for the same kind of checks.\n\nThose patches also return `-EPERM` when refusing to open or create the object and `-EOPNOTSUPP` from `mmap()`. Would that split work here too?\n\nThe new `#include` lines shouldn\u0027t be needed either: `\u003clinux/mm_types.h\u003e` already includes `\u003clinux/p3s/mm.h\u003e` through `\u003clinux/p3s.h\u003e`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4988ff901d7c9635d69338a4c41cf65473605672",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
