      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T06:57:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that 4KB processes shouldn\u0027t map these regions: `vfio_platform_mmap_mmio()` checks `req_start + req_len` against the region in kernel pages and ignores `vm_slice_off`, while since aosp/4368055 `remap_pfn_range()` starts at slice `vm_slice_off` of the first page. For example, mapping 16KB at offset 4KB of a 16KB region passes the check and maps the 4KB of MMIO after the region.\n\nBut as far as I can see `vfio_platform_mmap()` is only reached through `device-\u003eops-\u003emmap()` from `vfio_device_fops_mmap()`, which this patch already checks. Would it be OK to drop this hunk and the includes in this file?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4988ff901d7c9635d69338a4c41cf65473605672",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
