      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T06:57:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I can see the reads and writes don\u0027t depend on the caller\u0027s page size: `vfio_platform_read_mmio()` and `vfio_platform_write_mmio()` move 1, 2 or 4 bytes at a time with `ioread*()`/`iowrite*()` and `copy_to_user()`/`copy_from_user()`.\n\nThe same seems true for `vfio_device_fops_unl_ioctl()` and `vfio_group_fops_unl_ioctl()`, which exchange info structs, eventfds and fds. A device fd from `VFIO_GROUP_GET_DEVICE_FD` still can\u0027t be mapped because of the `vfio_device_fops_mmap()` check, and DMA mappings still go through the container ioctl check.\n\nWould it be OK to drop these four hunks?",
      "isAi": true,
